{"name":"Soft Vellum","hex":"#dddebe","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"soft","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily giving way under pressure.","Smooth and flexible; not rough, rugged, or harsh."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Be quiet; hold; stop; not so fast."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soft"},{"term":"vellum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of parchment paper made from the skin of a lamb, baby goat, or calf.","A writing paper of very high quality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vellum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vellum","blocks":[{"text":"Vellum is prepared animal skin or membrane, typically used as writing material. It is often distinguished from parchment, either by being made from calfskin, rather than the skin of other animals, or simply by being of a higher quality. Vellum is prepared for writing and printing on single pages, scrolls, and codices."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Magna_Carta_%28British_Library_Cotton_MS_Augustus_II.106%29.jpg/330px-Magna_Carta_%28British_Library_Cotton_MS_Augustus_II.106%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vellum"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/1638vellumlarge.jpg/500px-1638vellumlarge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/1638vellumlarge.jpg/500px-1638vellumlarge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A vellum deed dated 1638, with pendent seal attached","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1638vellumlarge.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Gutenberg_Bible.jpg/500px-Gutenberg_Bible.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src"